(6332937, 936976, 67723, '<td valign="top">Here''s a comment... There has been a lot of photos like this one in the fact that all it is, is a picture of a shoe or shoes in black and white set in front of a bland background with nothing but the title to make the photo mean anything. (other then a bland still life photo of a shoe) I haven''t been commenting on these photos but I suppose I should have to justify my mediocore/low vote. Obviously I don''t know who you are, but go ahead and have this comment. :) It''s something I need to learn myself, alot of my photos end up being bland as well and just don''t have much vision or creativity behind them. So this time I''m giving you a lower vote but I encourage you (and myself) to really get creative and add a story or impact to the photos we take. P.S. I''ve been thinking some and this sort of challenge may lend itself better if users would be able to submit a "photo story" with multiple photos. Photo stories then can include more "bland" individual images because they are used to tell the "story" and contribute to the collective impact and/or creativity. Hope this makes sense.. I don''t want to just slam your image since it''s not worthy of that, just describing my reason for voting it low in this challenge. Hope it helps!<br/> <br/>Justin</td>', 'Here''s a comment... There has been a lot of photos like this one in the fact that all it is, is a picture of a shoe or shoes in black and white set in front of a bland background with nothing but the title to make the photo mean anything. (other then a bland still life photo of a shoe) I haven''t been commenting on these photos but I suppose I should have to justify my mediocore/low vote. Obviously I don''t know who you are, but go ahead and have this comment. :) It''s something I need to learn myself, alot of my photos end up being bland as well and just don''t have much vision or creativity behind them. So this time I''m giving you a lower vote but I encourage you (and myself) to really get creative and add a story or impact to the photos we take. P.S. I''ve been thinking some and this sort of challenge may lend itself better if users would be able to submit a "photo story" with multiple photos. Photo stories then can include more "bland" individual images because they are used to tell the "story" and contribute to the collective impact and/or creativity. Hope this makes sense.. I don''t want to just slam your image since it''s not worthy of that, just describing my reason for voting it low in this challenge. Hope it helps! Justin', '2011-02-26 12:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
