(6338653, 937190, 112539, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I thought that toning down the contrast gave the dress shoes a duller, more lonely feel. From the comments... that was the wrong thing to do. If I had been allowed to take just the Keds and add contrast to them alone I would have to make them pop but this was basic editing. Is there a way to do that either in basic editing or in taking the photo that I could have done to create that effect? A trick with with lighting? Open for suggestions and critique.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-03-02 09:11:32.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I thought that toning down the contrast gave the dress shoes a duller, more lonely feel. From the comments... that was the wrong thing to do. If I had been allowed to take just the Keds and add contrast to them alone I would have to make them pop but this was basic editing. Is there a way to do that either in basic editing or in taking the photo that I could have done to create that effect? A trick with with lighting? Open for suggestions and critique.', '2011-03-02 09:08:43.000000', '2011-03-02 09:11:32.000000', 0),
(6338671, 937007, 54645, '<td valign="top">A rather brave entry to include feet. Excellent light and near excellent energy. I don''t think I critique your images very often, if ever, but I can see more emotion in this image with a shutter speed just slow enough to give some motion blur. This would have been further enhanced by your chosen title. An extension of your presentation.</td>', 'A rather brave entry to include feet. Excellent light and near excellent energy. I don''t think I critique your images very often, if ever, but I can see more emotion in this image with a shutter speed just slow enough to give some motion blur. This would have been further enhanced by your chosen title. An extension of your presentation.', '2011-03-02 09:38:16.000000', NULL, 0),
